    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec asked: on successful owner create, enqueue a welcome notification via the logger named `NOTIFY`, emitting a line containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` I made two edits:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification** in `addOwner(...)`, right after the successful-create audit events (and after the memberId has been assigned):\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome notification: ownerId={} memberId={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThis fires only on the success path (after `saveOwner` and id/memberId assignment), so the idempotency-replay and all validation-rejection paths correctly do not emit it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 it captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the fetched `memberId`.\n- Full suite: **262 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nThe observed log line confirms the behavior: `NOTIFY - welcome notification: ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`.",
